# D19 decision (Astra for the orchestrator, 2026-10-18): tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py, tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py, tests/test_execution_application.py, tests/test_external_owner_execution.py, tests/test_manager_assessment_ipc.py, tests/test_manager_completion_command.py, tests/test_manager_consumption_adoption.py, tests/test_manager_journey_command.py, tests/test_manager_service_continuation.py

Decision: LAND

- `tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py`: Removes reconciliation, readback and version assertions for the deleted lifecycle class (base `tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py:149`; base `src/otto/portfolio/lifecycle.py:46`). This matches the row’s explicit retirement and binding approval at `ops/requests.md:1444`. Surviving bridge replay and scope protections remain at `tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py:67` and `tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py:126`.
- `tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py`: Removes the retired lifecycle wrapper’s advisor-generation and assignment assertions (base `tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py:142`). The row explicitly deletes that subject; independent generation and wrong-recipient checks remain at `tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py:56` and `tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py:66`.
- `tests/test_execution_application.py`: Assertions are unchanged; calls migrate from the removed shortcut. Dispatch count, replay identity and changed-input rejection still detect regressions (`tests/test_execution_application.py:170`, `tests/test_execution_application.py:184`, `tests/test_execution_application.py:319`).
- `tests/test_external_owner_execution.py`: Assertions are unchanged. Migrated launches retain capture ordering, artifact contents and refusal to clean up without capture (`tests/test_external_owner_execution.py:227`, `tests/test_external_owner_execution.py:321`, `tests/test_external_owner_execution.py:389`).
- `tests/test_manager_assessment_ipc.py`: Only worker setup changes; success, serialized mutation and invocation-count assertions remain (`tests/test_manager_assessment_ipc.py:30`, `tests/test_manager_assessment_ipc.py:147`).
- `tests/test_manager_completion_command.py`: Only dispatch setup changes. Missing and tampered evidence must still prevent completion (`tests/test_manager_completion_command.py:166`, `tests/test_manager_completion_command.py:186`, `tests/test_manager_completion_command.py:194`).
- `tests/test_manager_consumption_adoption.py`: Two setup calls migrate without assertion changes. Parent/child identity and exactly-once consumption remain protected (`tests/test_manager_consumption_adoption.py:22`, `tests/test_manager_consumption_adoption.py:53`, `tests/test_manager_consumption_adoption.py:137`).
- `tests/test_manager_journey_command.py`: Only worker creation changes; exact occurrence, verdict schema and malformed-handle rejection assertions remain (`tests/test_manager_journey_command.py:49`, `tests/test_manager_journey_command.py:56`).
- `tests/test_manager_service_continuation.py`: Four worker-creation calls migrate; continuation identity, replay prevention, pending/unknown refusal and callback reuse assertions remain (`tests/test_manager_service_continuation.py:374`, `tests/test_manager_service_continuation.py:402`, `tests/test_manager_service_continuation.py:424`, `tests/test_manager_service_continuation.py:443`).

The shared helper departs from the prework’s explicit inline-migration instruction, but exactly reproduces the removed method’s control flow (`tests/execution_helpers.py:4`; base `src/otto/portfolio/execution.py:522`). It neither computes expected answers nor weakens these assertions. This approval covers D19 expectations; it does not certify full design compliance or passing gate tests.